From c4ba870584bbc3c22f65b2f579b02a5cadb008a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v11 <v11@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:57:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] v11: comparison narrowing, byte compares, FP-param XMM,
 ICC/ICX ILP distills

Distilled from ICC 2021.7.1 / ICX (godbolt) and GCC's byte-compare shapes,
plus the demanded FP-parameter register allocation.

1. U32 operand cast-type fix (lowering). emit_cast_val(x, I64, U32) hardcoded
   a wrong source type: the operand is already U32 (op_ty == U32 when
   common_ty == U32), so the cast was a type-lying identity that simplify
   could not fold and codegen emitted as a spurious mov per comparison
   operand. Now emits Cast(op_ty -> U32), which simplify folds away --
   removes the expat/sqlite mov-chains (one copy per comparison operand).

2. Comparison narrowing (simplify). Cmp(op, Cast(x, T->W), C, W) narrows to
   Cmp(op, x, C', T) when the extension preserves op's ordering and C fits in
   T: unsigned T zero-extends (Ult/Ule/Ugt/Uge + Eq/Ne), signed T
   sign-extends (Slt/... + Eq/Ne). Matches LLVM InstCombine's icmp-narrowing.

3. Byte/word compares (x86 emitter). emit_int_cmp_insn_typed and
   emit_int_cmp_replay_insn are now width-aware (cmpb/testb/cmpw/testw via
   cmp_width_info + typed_phys_reg_name), so a narrowed byte compares at its
   native width: the load + cmpb/testsil/jae shape GCC and ICX emit. Replaces
   the old I32/U32-vs-64bit boolean.

4. GPR simple-ALU LHS hint (live_range). Add/Sub/And/Or/Xor/Mul compute into
   the destination with the LHS pre-loaded (emit_alu_reg_direct), so the
   follow-hint generalizes from FP to GPR simple-ALU LHS edges -- the range
   fold's sub now lands in the cast's register with no copy.

5. FP-parameter XMM allocation + dead-param-store elimination.
   - ParamRef dests of FP type join the Phase 3 XMM scan.
   - find_dead_param_allocas marks a param alloca dead when its ParamRef dest
     has a stable home (callee-saved GPR or an XMM register).
   - emit_store_params pre-stores FloatReg args straight into the allocated
     XMM home (movss/movsd).
   - A param whose ParamRef was constant-propagated away (or is unused) is
     now dead, eliminating the entry spill (nbody's advance(0.01,...) no
     longer stores the folded dt; frame shrank 0xd8 to 0xc8).
   - A runtime FP param stays in XMM: dot(a,b) pre-stores both params into
     XMM registers with no slot round-trips.

6. Dead forwarding Cast/Copy skip (flag fusion). The fused chain's flag-
   neutral forwarding instructions read the never-materialized boolean, so
   their emitters now skip them (fused_forward_dests), removing the dead
   movsbq after each fused range check.

Measured (pinned, paired): bitops 1.91x -> 1.63x, gzip_crc32 1.45x -> 1.33x,
expat_xml_scan 2.89x -> 2.77x, sqlite_varint 2.09x -> 1.98x, nbody
3.47x -> 3.39x. Regression 133 passed / 0 failed, correctness 50/50,
intrinsics 3/3, 597 lib tests. New test v11_cmp_narrowing.
